What is a Biofilm Carrier for MBBR?
Biofilm carriers are essential components in Moving Bed Biofilm Reactor (MBBR) systems, serving as specialized plastic media that provides surface area for microbial colonization in wastewater treatment processes. These carrier elements - typically manufactured from resilient polymers like high-density polyethylene (HDPE) or polypropylene - are engineered to optimize biofilm development while maintaining structural integrity in demanding wastewater environments. Their unique geometries balance surface area expansion with hydraulic performance, enabling efficient biological treatment of both municipal sewage and industrial effluents.
